``` Name:        New device on the Management VLAN
    ATT&CK:      T1200 (Hardware Additions)
    Data:        index=netfw sourcetype=omada:controller (DHCP leases, by MAC)
                 + index=dns (DNS clients in Management, by IP) + lookup known_mgmt_devices
    Cron:        */15 * * * *
    Window:      -20m@m to -5m@m
    Severity:    high
    Tested with: a temporary LXC on VLAN 5 (2026-10-01). With DHCP it got no lease and the
                 controller logged nothing, so a DHCP-only rule was blind to it. With a static
                 IP and one DNS lookup, the DNS signal fired
    False positives: a legitimate new admin device. The daily baseline learns it,
                 so it alerts once ```
(index=netfw sourcetype=omada:controller "DHCP Server allocated" src_zone=management) OR (index=dns src_zone=management)
| eval device=if(index=="dns", src_ip, src_mac), kind=if(index=="dns", "dns_client_ip", "dhcp_mac")
| stats min(_time) AS first count AS events latest(src_ip) AS src_ip by device kind
| lookup known_mgmt_devices device OUTPUT first_seen AS known_since
| where isnull(known_since)
| eval detection="new_device_on_management", severity="high", attack="T1200", src_zone="management", _time=first
| eval summary="Unknown ".if(kind=="dhcp_mac", "MAC ".device." got a Management DHCP lease (".src_ip.")", "Management address ".device." started using DNS")
| fields _time detection severity attack summary src_ip src_zone device kind events
| collect index=soc_alerts source="detection:new_device_on_management"
